@* CreateUser.razor — Phase 6.2 (Admin/Manager user creation)

   Staff-facing user-creation page at route `/Admin/Users/Create`. Reached
   from the "Create user" button on /Admin/Users (added in this same
   phase). Role-gated to Admin / Manager via [Authorize(Roles=...)] as
   defense-in-depth. The page-level gate is the first cut; the command
   handlers enforce stricter rules server-side:
     - CreateCustomerCommand: [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]
     - CreateStaffCommand:    [RequireRoles(Admin)]  ← Managers CANNOT create staff

   PURPOSE:
     Lets admins/managers create new user accounts (staff or customer)
     via the UI, so test data can be seeded without DB access. Without
     this page, the only way to create users is via direct DB inserts
     or migrations — which blocks the full shopping-flow test (browse
     → cart → submit → /Sales) when no customer accounts exist.

   UNIFIED FORM (Customer + Staff):
     CreateCustomerCommand and CreateStaffCommand share 5 fields
     (WorkerId, FullName, Email, InitialPassword, Gender) and differ in:
       - Customer requires GroupName; Staff forbids it.
       - Customer always gets the "Customer" role; Staff requires an
         explicit Role selection (Employee / Manager / ReadOnly / Admin).
       - Customer creation: Manager or Admin. Staff creation: Admin only.
     A single unified form with a User Type toggle avoids ~80% code
     duplication and lets an admin flip between types without navigating
     back. When a Manager is signed in, the Staff option is HIDDEN and
     Customer is pre-selected + locked — this matches the server-side
     [RequireRoles(Admin)] on CreateStaffCommand (defense-in-depth).

   FORM FIELDS:
     1. User Type         (Customer / Staff toggle — Staff hidden from
                           Managers; selecting Staff clears GroupName,
                           selecting Customer clears StaffRole)
     2. Worker ID         (required, 1-100 chars — login identifier,
                           must be globally unique)
     3. Full Name         (required, 1-200 chars)
     4. Email             (required, valid email, max 256 chars)
     5. Initial Password  (required, 8-100 chars — show/hide toggle;
                           Identity's configured complexity rules are
                           the real authority)
     6. Gender            (Male / Female radio — 2-value enum per roadmap
                           Section 12.5; defaults to Male)
     7. Group Name        (required when Customer, max 100 chars;
                           HIDDEN when Staff)
     8. Staff Role        (Employee / Manager / ReadOnly / Admin
                           dropdown — HIDDEN when Customer)

   VALIDATION:
     - FluentValidation runs server-side via Wolverine's pipeline
       (CreateCustomerCommandValidator / CreateStaffCommandValidator).
       The validators produce the first wave of error messages
       (field-level, surfaced via EditContext validation).
     - The handlers do additional business-rule validation: WorkerId
       uniqueness (returns friendly "A user with worker ID 'X' already
       exists."), and Identity-level checks (duplicate email, weak
       password, role not seeded — surfaced via Result.Failure).
     - Client-side validation: minimal HTML5 required + min-length on
       password. The authoritative check is always server-side.

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN (CRITICAL):
     _isAdmin is computed via AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync()
     in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via ICurrentUserService.IsInRole. The
     ICurrentUserService reads from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext,
     which is NULL over the SignalR circuit in interactive Blazor Server
     mode. AuthStateProvider reads from the Blazor circuit's persistent
     auth state, which IS preserved across circuit interactions.

     Same pattern as AdminUsers.razor (Phase 6.1), Sales.razor (4.2),
     and SaleDetail.razor (4.3). The Wolverine command handlers ALSO
     enforce [RequireRoles] server-side as defense-in-depth.

   FORM SUBMISSION:
     - On valid submit: dispatch the appropriate command
       (CreateCustomerCommand or CreateStaffCommand) via Wolverine.
     - On success: toast + navigate to /Admin/Users (where the new user
       appears in the list — sorted by created-at desc, so newest first).
     - On failure: show result.Error inline at the top of the form.
       Field-level errors from FluentValidation are surfaced via
       EditContext validation.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<CreateUser> (Loc).
     Keys defined in CreateUser.en-US.resx + CreateUser.fa-IR.resx.
     RTL is handled at the html dir level by MainLayout.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Required — EditForm with OnValidSubmit. Blazor Server circuits
     already have an anti-forgery token established at circuit-start;
     EditForm validates it automatically. *@

@page "/Admin/Users/Create"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]
@using System.Globalization
@using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.CreateCustomer
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.CreateStaff
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<CreateUser> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .create-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .create-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            .form-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1.25rem;
            }

            .form-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                margin-top: 1rem;
            }

            .form-error {
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            .usertype-toggle {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .usertype-toggle .usertype-option {
                    flex: 1 1 200px;
                    min-width: 200px;
                }

            .gender-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 1.5rem;
                align-items: center;
            }

            .gender-option {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                cursor: pointer;
                user-select: none;
            }

            .password-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
            }

                .password-row .password-field {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                }

                .password-row .password-toggle {
                    flex: 0 0 auto;
                }

            /* Help panel on the right */
            .help-panel {
                position: sticky;
                top: 1rem;
            }

                .help-panel ul {
                    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
                    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    line-height: 1.7;
                }

                .help-panel li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .help-panel {
                    position: static;
                }
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Breadcrumb + back button ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToManageUsers"]"
                      Icon="arrow_back"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users", forceLoad: false))" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
        <RadzenIcon Icon="person_add" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Manager trying to create staff — locked-out notice ──
       When a Manager is signed in, the User Type toggle is locked to
       Customer (Staff is hidden). We render this small informational
       banner above the form so the manager understands why. Admins
       don't see it. *@
    @if (!_isAdmin)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ManagerScopeTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["ManagerScopeMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Info"
                     Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main form ── *@
    <div class="create-grid">
        @* LEFT — form fields *@
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
            <EditForm Model="@_model" OnValidSubmit="@HandleSubmitAsync" FormName="createUser">
                <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                @* Server-side error banner (e.g. "A user with worker ID 'X' already exists.") *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_submitError))
                {
                    <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                 Text="@_submitError"
                                 AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                 Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                 ShowIcon="true"
                                 Class="form-error" />
                }

                <div class="form-section">
                    @* ── User Type toggle ──
                       Admin: can pick Customer OR Staff.
                       Manager: locked to Customer (Staff option hidden —
                                server-side [RequireRoles(Admin)] is the
                                real guard; hiding the option is UX-only). *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["UserTypeLabel"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;" />
                        <div class="usertype-toggle">
                            <RadzenCard Variant="@(_model.UserType == UserType.Customer ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Outlined)"
                                        Class="usertype-option"
                                        Style="@($"padding: 0.75rem; cursor: pointer; border: 2px solid {GetToggleBorder(UserType.Customer)};")"
                                        @onclick="@(() => OnUserTypeChanged(UserType.Customer))">
                                <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="shopping_bag" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                                    <div>
                                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["UserTypeCustomer"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["UserTypeCustomerHint"]"
                                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin: 0;" />
                                    </div>
                                </RadzenStack>
                            </RadzenCard>

                            @if (_isAdmin)
                            {
                                <RadzenCard Variant="@(_model.UserType == UserType.Staff ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Outlined)"
                                            Class="usertype-option"
                                            Style="@($"padding: 0.75rem; cursor: pointer; border: 2px solid {GetToggleBorder(UserType.Staff)};")"
                                            @onclick="@(() => OnUserTypeChanged(UserType.Staff))">
                                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="badge" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                                        <div>
                                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["UserTypeStaff"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["UserTypeStaffHint"]"
                                                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin: 0;" />
                                        </div>
                                    </RadzenStack>
                                </RadzenCard>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Worker ID ── *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldWorkerId"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.WorkerId"
                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldWorkerIdPlaceholder"]"
                                           TValue="string"
                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                        </RadzenFormField>
                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                            @Loc["WorkerIdHint"]
                        </RadzenText>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Full Name ── *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldFullName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.FullName"
                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldFullNamePlaceholder"]"
                                           TValue="string"
                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                        </RadzenFormField>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Email ── *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldEmail"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.Email"
                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldEmailPlaceholder"]"
                                           TValue="string"
                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                        </RadzenFormField>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Initial Password (with show/hide toggle) ── *@
                    <div>
                        <div class="password-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldPassword"]" Class="password-field" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextBox Value="_model.InitialPassword"
                                               ValueChanged="@OnPasswordChanged"
                                               Type="@(_showPassword ? "text" : "password")"
                                               Placeholder="@Loc["FieldPasswordPlaceholder"]"
                                               TValue="string"
                                               Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <RadzenButton Icon="@(_showPassword ? "visibility_off" : "visibility")"
                                          title="@(_showPassword ? Loc["PasswordHide"] : Loc["PasswordShow"])"
                                          aria-label="@(_showPassword ? Loc["PasswordHide"] : Loc["PasswordShow"])"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Click="@TogglePasswordVisibility" />
                        </div>
                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                            @Loc["PasswordHint"]
                        </RadzenText>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Gender ──
                       2-value enum per roadmap Section 12.5 (Male / Female).
                       Radio buttons (not dropdown) since there are only 2
                       options and radio is faster to scan. Defaults to Male
                       (the Domain factory default). *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["FieldGender"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;" />
                        <InputRadioGroup @bind-Value="_model.Gender" TValue="Domain.Users.Gender">
                            <div class="gender-row">
                                <label class="gender-option">
                                    <InputRadio Value="@(Domain.Users.Gender.Male)" />
                                    <span>@Loc["GenderMale"]</span>
                                </label>
                                <label class="gender-option">
                                    <InputRadio Value="@(Domain.Users.Gender.Female)" />
                                    <span>@Loc["GenderFemale"]</span>
                                </label>
                            </div>
                        </InputRadioGroup>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Group Name (Customer only) ──
                       Required for Customer (enforced server-side by the
                       validator and Domain invariant). Hidden for Staff —
                       staff users have null GroupName by design. *@
                    @if (_model.UserType == UserType.Customer)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldGroupName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.GroupName"
                                               Placeholder="@Loc["FieldGroupNamePlaceholder"]"
                                               TValue="string"
                                               Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                                @Loc["GroupNameHint"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        </div>
                    }

                    @* ── Staff Role (Staff only, Admin only) ──
                       Admin selects which staff role to assign at creation
                       (Employee / Manager / ReadOnly / Admin). The Customer
                       role is NOT in this list — staff accounts are never
                       customers at creation time. (A manager or employee
                       who wants to buy on their own behalf gets the Customer
                       role added later via AssignUserRoleCommand.)

                       BINDING PATTERN:
                       We bind the dropdown to the PRIMITIVE role string
                       (TValue="string"), not to the complex StaffRoleOption
                       object. This matches the sibling pattern in
                       CreateProduct.razor (TValue="Guid?") and
                       AdminUsers.razor (TValue="ActivityFilter" enum).
                       RadzenDropDown's ValueProperty/TextProperty handle the
                       complex-to-primitive mapping; the binding itself
                       operates on the primitive key only. *@
                    @if (_model.UserType == UserType.Staff && _isAdmin)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldStaffRole"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="_model.StaffRole"
                                                Data="_staffRoleOptions"
                                                TValue="string"
                                                TextProperty="Label"
                                                ValueProperty="Value"
                                                Placeholder="@Loc["StaffRolePlaceholder"]"
                                                Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                                @Loc["StaffRoleHint"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        </div>
                    }

                    @* ── Form actions ── *@
                    <div class="form-actions">
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                      Icon="close"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Disabled="@_isSubmitting"
                                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users", forceLoad: false))" />
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SubmitButton"]"
                                      Icon="save"
                                      ButtonType="ButtonType.Submit"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                      Disabled="@_isSubmitting" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </EditForm>
        </RadzenCard>

        @* RIGHT — help panel (sticky on desktop) *@
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="help-panel" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem" Style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="help_outline" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["HelpTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
            </RadzenStack>
            <ul>
                <li>@Loc["HelpWorkerIdUnique"]</li>
                <li>@Loc["HelpEmail"]</li>
                <li>@Loc["HelpPassword"]</li>
                <li>@Loc["HelpGender"]</li>
                <li>@Loc["HelpGroupName"]</li>
                <li>@Loc["HelpStaffRole"]</li>
                <li>@Loc["HelpInitialPassword"]</li>
            </ul>
        </RadzenCard>
    </div>
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Form model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// View-model for the create-user form. Holds fields for BOTH Customer
    /// and Staff creation in one flat object — the User Type toggle
    /// determines which fields are shown and which command is dispatched
    /// at submit time. Staff-only fields (StaffRole) and customer-only
    /// fields (GroupName) are simply ignored when the other type is
    /// selected.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class CreateUserFormModel
    {
        // Validation attributes mirror the union of CreateStaffCommandValidator
        // and CreateCustomerCommandValidator rules. Fields used by BOTH
        // validators (WorkerId, FullName, Email, InitialPassword, Gender) get
        // the shared rules. Fields used by only one (GroupName = customer-only,
        // StaffRole = staff-only) are validated conditionally in HandleSubmitAsync
        // (the existing manual checks at lines ~600-610 already do this and
        // produce localized Error_GroupNameRequired / Error_StaffRoleRequired
        // messages — we don't want to duplicate that logic with [Required]
        // because the attribute would fire even when the wrong UserType is
        // selected).
        //
        // The FluentValidation validators on the commands still run server-side
        // as defense-in-depth. Localized messages will be wired in Phase 7
        // item D (FluentValidation LanguageManager); for now, DataAnnotations'
        // default English messages are shown by <ValidationMessage> if added
        // to the markup.

        public UserType UserType { get; set; } = UserType.Customer;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Worker ID is required.")]
        [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "Worker ID cannot exceed 100 characters.")]
        public string WorkerId { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Full name is required.")]
        [StringLength(200, ErrorMessage = "Full name cannot exceed 200 characters.")]
        public string FullName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Email is required.")]
        [StringLength(256, ErrorMessage = "Email cannot exceed 256 characters.")]
        [EmailAddress(ErrorMessage = "Email must be a valid email address.")]
        public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Initial password is required.")]
        [StringLength(100, MinimumLength = 8, ErrorMessage = "Password must be between 8 and 100 characters.")]
        public string InitialPassword { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        // Gender enum — default Male. EnumDataType validates that the value
        // is a defined member (mirrors FluentValidation's IsInEnum).
        [EnumDataType(typeof(Domain.Users.Gender), ErrorMessage = "Gender must be a valid value (Male or Female).")]
        public Domain.Users.Gender Gender { get; set; } = Domain.Users.Gender.Male;

        // Customer-only — validated conditionally in HandleSubmitAsync
        // (Error_GroupNameRequired). No [Required] here because that would
        // fire even when UserType is Staff.
        [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "Group name cannot exceed 100 characters.")]
        public string GroupName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        /// <summary>
        /// The selected staff role's string value (e.g. "Employee",
        /// "Manager", "ReadOnly", "Admin"). Null when no role has been
        /// picked yet OR when UserType is Customer.
        ///
        /// We bind the PRIMITIVE string here (not the complex
        /// StaffRoleOption object) to match the sibling dropdown pattern.
        /// The Label is looked up from _staffRoleOptions at display time
        /// (e.g. for the success toast).
        ///
        /// Staff-only — validated conditionally in HandleSubmitAsync
        /// (Error_StaffRoleRequired). No [Required] here because that would
        /// fire even when UserType is Customer.
        /// </summary>
        public string? StaffRole { get; set; }
    }

    private enum UserType
    {
        Customer,
        Staff
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Strongly-typed staff-role option for the dropdown. The Value is the
    /// string role name as expected by CreateStaffCommand (matches the
    /// Roles constants). The Label is localized for display.
    ///
    /// BINDING NOTE:
    ///   The dropdown binds to the PRIMITIVE string Value (TValue="string"),
    ///   NOT to this complex object. The StaffRoleOption list is only used
    ///   as the Data source — RadzenDropDown's ValueProperty="Value" /
    ///   TextProperty="Label" handle the complex-to-primitive mapping.
    ///   This matches the sibling pattern in CreateProduct.razor (TValue="Guid?"
    ///   with CategoryDto data) and AdminUsers.razor (TValue="ActivityFilter"
    ///   with ActivityFilterOption data).
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class StaffRoleOption
    {
        public string Value { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    private CreateUserFormModel _model = new();

    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private bool _isAdmin;
    private bool _isSubmitting;
    private string _submitError = string.Empty;
    private bool _showPassword;

    private List<StaffRoleOption> _staffRoleOptions = new();

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Resolve the current user's Admin role via the Blazor auth state
        // (NOT ICurrentUserService.IsInRole — see file-header comment).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;
            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _isAdmin stays false. Managers can still create
            // customers; only the Staff toggle is hidden.
            _isAdmin = false;
        }

        // Populate the staff-role dropdown options. The Value strings
        // match the Roles constants exactly (verified at compile time via
        // nameof where possible, but RadzenDropDown's ValueProperty uses
        // reflection, so we just pass the string).
        _staffRoleOptions = new List<StaffRoleOption>
        {
            new() { Value = Roles.Employee, Label = Loc["RoleEmployee"] },
            new() { Value = Roles.Manager,  Label = Loc["RoleManager"] },
            new() { Value = Roles.ReadOnly, Label = Loc["RoleReadOnly"] },
            new() { Value = Roles.Admin,    Label = Loc["RoleAdmin"] }
        };

        // If a Manager is signed in, lock the User Type to Customer.
        // (Admins see both options and can pick either.)
        if (!_isAdmin)
        {
            _model.UserType = UserType.Customer;
        }
    }

    // ── Handlers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles between Customer and Staff user types. Clears the
    /// type-specific fields (GroupName for Staff, StaffRole for Customer)
    /// so the form doesn't carry stale values across the toggle.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnUserTypeChanged(UserType newType)
    {
        if (_model.UserType == newType) return Task.CompletedTask;

        _model.UserType = newType;

        if (newType == UserType.Staff)
        {
            _model.GroupName = string.Empty;
        }
        else
        {
            _model.StaffRole = null;
        }

        // Clear any stale submit error from a previous attempt.
        _submitError = string.Empty;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles the password visibility between masked and plaintext.
    /// Purely a UX affordance — no validation implications.
    /// </summary>
    private Task TogglePasswordVisibility()
    {
        _showPassword = !_showPassword;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Bound to the password field's ValueChanged callback so we can
    /// toggle the input type between Text and Password without losing
    /// the value (using @bind-Value with a type change can drop the
    /// current input).
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnPasswordChanged(string value)
    {
        _model.InitialPassword = value ?? string.Empty;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the CSS color for the user-type toggle border. Both options
    /// use the primary color as their border; the actual visual cue for
    /// which type is selected comes from the RadzenCard's Variant
    /// (Variant.Filled for selected, Variant.Outlined for unselected).
    /// This helper exists for future customization (e.g. dim the
    /// unselected border) but currently returns the same value for both
    /// types to keep the visual hierarchy driven by the Variant alone.
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetToggleBorder(UserType type)
        => "var(--rz-primary)";

    // ── Submit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleSubmitAsync()
    {
        _submitError = string.Empty;

        // Defense-in-depth: if a Manager somehow ended up with UserType=Staff
        // (e.g. they were an Admin, picked Staff, then had their role
        // revoked — extremely unlikely), block the submit client-side.
        // The server-side [RequireRoles(Admin)] on CreateStaffCommand is
        // the real guard; this just gives a friendlier error.
        if (_model.UserType == UserType.Staff && !_isAdmin)
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_ManagerCannotCreateStaff"];
            return;
        }

        // Staff requires a role selection.
        if (_model.UserType == UserType.Staff && _model.StaffRole is null)
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_StaffRoleRequired"];
            return;
        }

        // Customer requires a non-empty GroupName.
        if (_model.UserType == UserType.Customer && string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_model.GroupName))
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_GroupNameRequired"];
            return;
        }

        _isSubmitting = true;

        try
        {
            Result<Guid> result;

            if (_model.UserType == UserType.Customer)
            {
                var command = new CreateCustomerCommand(
                    WorkerId: _model.WorkerId.Trim(),
                    FullName: _model.FullName.Trim(),
                    GroupName: _model.GroupName.Trim(),
                    Email: _model.Email.Trim(),
                    InitialPassword: _model.InitialPassword,
                    Gender: _model.Gender);

                result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);
            }
            else
            {
                var command = new CreateStaffCommand(
                    WorkerId: _model.WorkerId.Trim(),
                    FullName: _model.FullName.Trim(),
                    Email: _model.Email.Trim(),
                    InitialPassword: _model.InitialPassword,
                    Role: _model.StaffRole!,
                    Gender: _model.Gender);

                result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);
            }

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                // For the Staff success toast, look up the localized role
                // label (e.g. "Employee" → "کارمند") so the Persian toast
                // doesn't leak the Latin role constant.
                var staffRoleLabel = _model.StaffRole is null
                    ? string.Empty
                    : _staffRoleOptions.FirstOrDefault(o => o.Value == _model.StaffRole)?.Label ?? _model.StaffRole;

                var successMsg = _model.UserType == UserType.Customer
                    ? string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["CreateSuccessCustomer"], _model.FullName)
                    : string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["CreateSuccessStaff"], _model.FullName, staffRoleLabel);

                await Toast.Success(successMsg, summary: Loc["CreateSuccessTitle"]);

                // Navigate back to the admin user list — the new user
                // appears at the top (sorted by created-at desc, assuming
                // the list query orders that way; if not, the user can
                // search by worker ID).
                Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users", forceLoad: false);
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains a user-friendly message from the
                // handler — e.g.:
                //   "A user with worker ID 'EMP-123' already exists."
                //   "User name 'EMP-123' is already taken." (Identity)
                //   "Email 'foo@bar.com' is already taken." (Identity)
                //   "Passwords must have at least one non-alphanumeric character." (Identity)
                _submitError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericCreate"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_GenericCreate"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }
}